# tools/kit-boundary.allow — where the app may touch the GPU or a numerics framework (decision D15).
#
# One line per file: <path><TAB><modules the file may import, comma-separated; `-` for a .metal file><TAB><reason>.
# tools/check-kit-boundary.sh fails on a gated import (Accelerate, vecLib, Metal, MetalKit, MetalPerformanceShaders*,
# BNNS, simd) in a file or module not listed here, on any vDSP / cblas / vImage / LAPACK / vForce / BNNS / MPS symbol
# anywhere, and on a .metal file not listed. Numerics belong in the kits; a new line here needs a reason that is display,
# not science, or a lineage/marks record (app-side provenance).

# The display pipeline is MacEMUI's (its Colormaps.metal); the app holds no .metal file. The test of its export twin:
macTEMTests/ImageExportGPUTests.swift	Metal	GPU image export vs CPU rendering

# SEM: the float32 GPU paths of two numeric ports in TEMCore.
Sources/TEMCore/SEM/MasterPattern/MasterPatternProjectionMetal.swift	Metal	SEM master pattern projection: the float32 GPU path of a numeric port that lives in TEMCore because the SEM program changes no kit; checked against the float64 CPU path
Sources/TEMCore/SEM/Indexing/DictionaryIndexingMetal.swift	Metal	SEM dictionary indexing: the float32 GPU matrix product of a numeric port that lives in TEMCore because the SEM program changes no kit; checked against the float64 CPU path
